@model RenoTrack.Website.Site.ServiceCardsModel
@using RenoTrack.Website.Site
@inject MarketingSite Marketing
@*
    Service cards (D105; re-drawn in Slice 5v, D107): an index numeral, the service name, its summary and the
    first of its offerings, in the order given.

    The link sits on the heading and its accessible name is the service name alone; a CSS pseudo-element stretches it
    over the card, so there is no second "Mehr erfahren" link and nothing interactive nested inside the link. The
    footer line is decoration with no text of its own, for the same reason.

    The index span is empty and aria-hidden: a CSS counter draws it. It is the card's position in the list, never a
    claim about anything, and a screen reader already hears the list.

    The heading level is the caller's (ServiceCardsModel), so no page skips a level. Written out as two branches rather
    than a computed tag name, which would need Html.Raw.

    Photos (D106, S5-7) appear only when every service on the site has one — decided once at startup, so the homepage,
    the overview and "Weitere Leistungen" always agree. The photo sits outside the link and is not focusable; its alt
    text describes the photo, not the service name the heading already announces. Lazy, because cards are below the
    hero. A card's geometry is the same in both states: the photo is a slot above an otherwise identical card, so
    enabling photography changes what a card shows and never how the grid is composed.
*@
<ul class="page-cards">
    @foreach (var service in Model.Services)
    {
        var href = MarketingSite.ServicePath(service);
        var image = Marketing.ServiceCardImagesEnabled ? Marketing.ImageFor(service) : null;
        var offerings = service.Offerings.Take(3).ToList();
        <li class="page-card page-card-linked@(image is null ? "" : " page-card-with-image")">
            @if (image is not null)
            {
                <div class="page-card-media">
                    <partial name="@SiteLayout.Picture" model="new PictureModel(image, PictureSizes.Card, PictureLoading.Lazy)" />
                </div>
            }
            <span class="page-card-index" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            @if (Model.HeadingLevel == 2)
            {
                <h2 class="page-card-title"><a class="page-card-link" href="@href">@service.Name</a></h2>
            }
            else
            {
                <h3 class="page-card-title"><a class="page-card-link" href="@href">@service.Name</a></h3>
            }
            <p class="page-card-text">@service.Summary</p>
            @if (offerings.Count > 0)
            {
                <ul class="page-card-offerings">
                    @foreach (var offering in offerings)
                    {
                        <li class="page-card-offering">@offering</li>
                    }
                </ul>
            }
            <span class="page-card-go" aria-hidden="true">Zur Leistung</span>
        </li>
    }
</ul>
